  "summary_en": "Japan's Second AI Basic Plan under the 2025 AI Act sets four pillars: accelerating AI deployment, strengthening development, leading governance, and building an AI-powered society. It prioritises agentic, vertical and physical AI (robots, autonomous driving) while advancing agile, largely voluntary governance, AISI evaluation and international cooperation.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Prioritises vertical AI and physical AI, including AI robotics, robot foundation models and autonomous driving, as Japan's winning strategy.",
   "Adopts 'responsible agile governance' combining institutional, technical and organizational management responses.",
   "Strengthens the AI Safety Institute for evaluation of frontier AI and cyber risks.",
   "Commits to examining allocation of responsibility for AI harms and reviewing existing regulations.",
   "Pursues international standards for autonomous driving, Hiroshima AI Process, and balanced military AI discussions."
  ],
